---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import LarchPlanningInteractions from '../components/LarchPlanningInteractions.astro';
import {trails} from '../data/trails';
import {larchRouteChoices,larchFilterOptions,buildLarchPlan,larchFaqs,larchSources,larchReviewedAt} from '../data/larchPlanning';
const initial=buildLarchPlan();
const routes=larchRouteChoices.map(choice=>{
  const trail=trails.find(trail=>trail.slug===choice.id);
  if(!trail?.routeVerified||trail.sourceReview?.status!=='reviewed')throw new Error('Missing reviewed larch route: '+choice.id);
  return {...choice,trail};
});
const labels={area:'Where will the walk start?',duration:'Published return hiking estimate',season:'Which kind of trip are you planning?'};
const grade={easy:'Easy',moderate:'Moderate',challenging:'Difficult'};
---
<BaseLayout title="Larch Season in Banff — Timing, Trails & Autumn Planner" description="Compare five sourced Banff larch hiking profiles by trailhead and return estimate. Plan seasonal transport, route endpoints and changing autumn conditions with current official source links." lastUpdated={larchReviewedAt}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:larchFaqs.map(faq=>({'@type':'Question',name:faq.question,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:faq.answer}}))}).replace(/</g,'\\u003c')} />
  <div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Larch Season'}]} /></div>
  <section class="larch-hero"><div class="container"><span class="badge">An autumn worth planning</span><h1>Larch Season in Banff</h1><p>Golden trees are one part of the day. Choose the right trailhead, the walk you actually want, and a return that still works when the mountains change the plan.</p><a class="larch-button" href="#larch-planner">Find your autumn route ↓</a></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container larch-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">A short, variable season</span><h2>Leave room for the season to surprise you</h2><p>Banff &amp; Lake Louise Tourism describes typical golden larch colour from <strong>late September into early October</strong>. Treat that as a planning window, rather than the peak date for every trail. Wind, snow and the year’s weather can change what you find.</p><p>Build a trip you will enjoy with green needles, patchy colour or cloud as well as the photograph you hope for. A forest walk, a higher pass and an overnight lodge journey have different commitments. <a href={larchSources.fall} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the destination’s autumn guidance ↗</a></p></div><aside class="larch-note"><h3>Before you commit to a trail</h3><p>Use the official trail report, notices and forecast close to departure. A report’s observation date matters; a clear road, a photograph or an autumn calendar date does not describe the trail above it.</p><a href={larchSources.reports} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check Parks Canada trail reports ↗</a><a href={larchSources.notices} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read current park notices ↗</a></aside></div></section>
  <section class="section larch-planner-section" id="larch-planner" aria-labelledby="larch-planner-title"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-header"><span class="eyebrow">Start with the whole walk</span><h2 id="larch-planner-title">Find a route to investigate</h2><p>Five published summer profiles, with different starts and endpoints. Return estimates describe hiking, not a complete door-to-door itinerary.</p></div>
    <form id="larch-form" hidden>{Object.entries(larchFilterOptions).map(([key,options])=><label for={`larch-${key}`}>{labels[key as keyof typeof labels]}<select id={`larch-${key}`} name={`larch_${key}`}>{options.map(([value,label])=><option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></label>)}<div class="larch-actions"><button type="submit">Show routes</button><button type="reset">Show all</button></div></form>
    <p id="larch-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">{initial.summary}</p><p id="larch-season-note" class="larch-note">{initial.note}</p><p class="larch-small">Filters compare the published starting area and the upper end of Parks Canada’s summer return estimate. They do not rate a route for your group, forecast foliage, or confirm opening, parking or a shuttle seat.</p>
    <noscript><p>All five route profiles and their direct source links are available below. Compare the figures and journey notes without the filters.</p></noscript>
    <aside id="larch-empty" class="larch-note" hidden><h3>No listed profile matches both choices</h3><p>Try another starting area or return estimate, or show all five. This small comparison does not cover every route in the park. A shorter time estimate does not make a different trail easier.</p></aside>
    <div class="larch-grid">{routes.map(route=><article data-larch-route={route.id} id={`larch-${route.id}`} class="larch-card"><span class="eyebrow">{grade[route.trail.difficulty]}</span><h3>{route.title}</h3><p>{route.idea}</p><dl><div><dt>Distance basis</dt><dd>{route.trail.distance}</dd></div><div><dt>Published ascent</dt><dd>{route.trail.elevationGain}</dd></div><div><dt>Summer return estimate</dt><dd>{route.trail.time}</dd></div><div><dt>Trailhead</dt><dd>{route.trail.trailhead}</dd></div></dl><p>{route.boundary}</p><a class="larch-profile" href={`/trails/${route.id}/`}>Explore the full trail profile →</a><details><summary>Transport, season &amp; source checks</summary><p>{route.trail.transitRoute||route.trail.accessNote}</p><p>{route.trail.winterNote}</p><p>The figures above describe the stated endpoint. Add your actual approach, breaks and return connection before deciding whether the day fits.</p><ul><li><a href={larchSources.hiking} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Parks Canada detailed summer profile ↗</a></li><li><a href={route.larchSource} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Published larch context ↗</a></li></ul></details></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container larch-intro"><div><h2>Resolve the trailhead before the hotel-to-hike plan</h2><p>Larch Valley and Sentinel Pass start at Moraine Lake. Saddleback starts at the Lake Louise lakeshore, which is separate from the village and ski resort. Taylor Lake starts at a highway-side day-use area. Healy Pass starts at Sunshine’s lower base, rather than the upper village reached by gondola.</p><p>Moraine Lake Road is closed to personal vehicles year-round. Parks Canada’s published 2026 lake shuttle season ended October 12; do not carry that timetable into another year. Confirm the actual service, check-in location, reservation and last return for your trip before making a hike depend on it.</p><a href={larchSources.access} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check official lake transport ↗</a></div><aside class="larch-note"><h3>A plan for snow changes the outing</h3><p>Parks Canada identifies avalanche exposure and advises against mid-October to mid-June travel on the Lake Louise-area routes in this comparison. This includes Taylor Lake, Larch Valley, Saddleback and Sentinel Pass. Healy Pass needs its own snow-season assessment.</p><p>Changing the season setting above does not convert these summer profiles into winter hikes. Keep an alternative day that suits the actual conditions.</p><a href={larchSources.avalanche} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read Parks’ mountain-safety information ↗</a></aside></div></section>
  <section class="section larch-next"><div class="container"><h2>Build the rest of your autumn trip</h2><div class="larch-next-grid"><a href="/towns/lake-louise/"><strong>Stay near the right starting point →</strong><span>Compare the village, lakeshore and wider Lake Louise journey.</span></a><a href="/blog/skoki-lodge-guide/"><strong>Make Skoki a separate lodge trip →</strong><span>Resolve the booking, season, approach and overnight arrangements.</span></a><a href="/packing-list/?season=summer&activities=hiking"><strong>Prepare your hiking kit →</strong><span>Build a checklist for the outing and the changing weather.</span></a><a href="/what-to-do-today/"><strong>Keep another kind of day in mind →</strong><span>Compare outings by your base, time and interests.</span></a></div><p class="larch-small">The stay guide contains disclosed accommodation affiliate links. A referral or a nearby hotel booking does not include a trail reservation, transport or a Skoki Lodge stay.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container larch-faq"><h2 id="larch-faq-title">Larch trip questions</h2>{larchFaqs.map(faq=><details><summary>{faq.question}</summary><p>{faq.answer}</p></details>)}<p class="larch-small">Selected route and seasonal sources reviewed October 29, 2026. These are source-dated planning notes, not live colour or trail observations. Parks Canada supplies the route profiles; Banff &amp; Lake Louise Tourism supplies the broad autumn context.</p></div></section>
  <LarchPlanningInteractions />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .larch-hero{background:var(--color-primary);color:#fff;padding:4rem 0}.larch-hero .container{max-width:950px}.larch-hero h1{color:#fff;font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4.2rem);line-height:1.1;margin:1rem 0}.larch-hero p{font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.8;max-width:740px}.larch-button{display:inline-block;background:var(--color-accent);color:var(--color-primary);padding:.85rem 1.25rem;border-radius:8px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;margin-top:1rem}.eyebrow{font-size:.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;font-weight:700;color:var(--color-primary)}.larch-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.5fr 1fr;gap:2rem;align-items:start}.larch-intro p{line-height:1.85}.larch-note{background:var(--color-bg-alt);padding:1.4rem;border-radius:12px;line-height:1.8}.larch-note h3{font-size:1.15rem}.larch-note a{display:block;margin-top:.75rem}.larch-planner-section{background:var(--color-bg-alt)}#larch-form{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;background:#fff;padding:1.3rem;border-radius:12px}#larch-form[hidden],#larch-empty[hidden],.larch-card[hidden]{display:none}#larch-form label{font-weight:700;font-size:.85rem}#larch-form select{display:block;width:100%;margin-top:.6rem;padding:.75rem;border:1px solid #aab1ab;border-radius:6px;background:#fff;color:var(--color-text);font:inherit}.larch-actions{display:flex;gap:.7rem;grid-column:1/-1;flex-wrap:wrap}.larch-actions button{border:1px solid var(--color-primary);border-radius:6px;background:var(--color-primary);color:#fff;padding:.7rem 1.2rem;font:inherit;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}.larch-actions button[type=reset]{background:#fff;color:var(--color-primary)}#larch-status{font-weight:700;margin:1.25rem 0}.larch-small{font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;color:var(--color-text-light)}.larch-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.25rem;margin-top:1.5rem}.larch-card{padding:1.6rem;background:#fff;border-radius:12px;border-top:4px solid var(--color-primary);box-shadow:var(--shadow)}.larch-card h3{font-size:1.45rem;margin:.5rem 0 .8rem}.larch-card p,.larch-card li{line-height:1.8}.larch-card dl{margin:1.2rem 0}.larch-card dl div{padding:.55rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e8e4}.larch-card dt{font-size:.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--color-text-light)}.larch-card dd{margin:.25rem 0 0;line-height:1.7}.larch-profile{display:inline-block;font-weight:700;margin:.75rem 0}.larch-card details{margin-top:.75rem;border-top:1px solid #d5dcd3;padding-top:1rem}.larch-card summary,.larch-faq summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700;line-height:1.7}.larch-card ul{padding-left:1.2rem}.larch-next{background:var(--color-bg-alt)}.larch-next-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.larch-next-grid a{display:block;background:#fff;border-radius:10px;padding:1.4rem;text-decoration:none;color:var(--color-primary)}.larch-next-grid span{display:block;margin-top:.7rem;line-height:1.75;font-size:.9rem}.larch-faq{max-width:900px}.larch-faq details{padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid #d5dcd3;border-radius:10px;margin:1rem 0}.larch-faq p{line-height:1.85}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:768px){.larch-hero{padding:2.8rem 0}.larch-intro,.larch-grid,.larch-next-grid,#larch-form{grid-template-columns:1fr}.larch-card{padding:1.25rem}.larch-intro{gap:1rem}}
</style>
